        "causedByEventId": "4de8262a-50c3-431e-8900-cbd7586afd70",
        "text": "**Not published. The gate is red, so the release stopped before any version bump, tag or publish.**\n\n**Git vs npm:** npm `latest` and `package.json` are both 0.87.0, and the `v0.87.0` tag is the last release. HEAD is 64dbfb0, 76 commits past that tag. They include `feat(...)` commits, so the bump would be **minor, 0.88.0**.\n\n**Gate (run in a clean worktree at HEAD, since the main tree is dirty):**\n- `typecheck` passed.\n- `test:unit` had 46 failures across 16 files (4847 passed).\n\nTwo separate causes:\n\n1. **`prepublishOnly` is broken at HEAD.** It runs `npm run build:project-pages`, and that fails with `Could not resolve src/renderer/lib/projectPages/render.tsx`. Commits `00bbdcc`, `f9c63b4` and `5cc32fa` removed the old render pipeline, but `web/project-pages/build-renderer.mjs` still points at it. Even with the gate skipped, `npm publish` would fail at that step.\n   - Related failures, which also fail in the main tree: `scripts/__tests__/package-files.test.cjs`, `web/project-pages/__tests__/publish-gate.test.cjs`, and 17 in `tests/unit/usage-dashboard.spec.ts`. The dashboard spec imports `session-manager-operations/project-pages/output/dashboard/dashboard.js`, which doesn't exist in a clean checkout.\n2. **HEAD's tests and source are out of step.** The scheduler and admin-route tests fail in the clean worktree but pass in the main tree, where those files are modified but uncommitted. They are `prdAdminRoutes`, `scheduler-reap-dead-running-jobs` (15 failures), `looks-done`, `inplace-salvage`, `quiet-machine-lease`, `shared-tree-guard`, `worktree-cap-defer` and `prd-missing-skip`. The files affected (`scheduler.cjs`, `prdLocations.cjs`, `scheduleJobTransitions.cjs` and others) are modified but not committed. Publishing HEAD as-is would ship a scheduler that doesn't match its own tests.\n\nI couldn't tell whether the rest are real or environmental. `opsRootAbsoluteCwd` fails only in worktrees (a known hazard), and `queueHistory` and the three `telemetry*` files didn't ge…",
        "id": "pevt-mu815hq6-81",
        "promptSessionId": "builder-check-git-vs-the-published-package-for-t-f5aa9d5c",
        "at": "2026-09-19T06:52:25.470Z"
      },
      {
        "kind": "response",
        "causedByEventId": "pevt-mu815hq6-81",
        "text": "The release is still blocked, and nothing has changed since my last report.\n\n- **HEAD is unchanged:** it is still `64dbfb0`, and there is no new commit. The scheduler work you mean is still uncommitted in the working tree: `scheduler.cjs`, `prdLocations.cjs`, `scheduleJobTransitions.cjs`, `index.cjs`, `api.d.ts`, `NewEpicCard.tsx`, the modified scheduler tests, and a new `scheduler-reconcile-cwd-preserve.test.cjs`. The release is cut from a tag, so uncommitted changes can't ship. HEAD's tests and source are still out of step, which is what made the clean-worktree gate fail.\n- **`prepublishOnly` is still broken independent of the scheduler:** `build:project-pages` still points at `render.tsx`, which is gone. `npm publish` would fail on that step even if the scheduler work were committed.\n\nI haven't committed the scheduler changes or touched the project-pages build, so no release was attempted. The changes come from other Epics' jobs, and I can't tell from here whether they are a complete, verified set.\n\nTo unblock, I need two things:\n1. Your go-ahead to commit the scheduler working-tree changes to `main` (or a ready commit from that Epic).\n2. A fix for the project-pages build, which is `/develop` work in this project. Either delete `web/project-pages/build-renderer.mjs` and `build-logic.mjs`, drop them from `prepublishOnly`, and remove the tests that depend on them, or restore a working build entry.\n\nAfter both land, `/builder` re-runs the gate and publishes 0.88.0. Because it is a minor bump, the manual step will also need to check the Field Manual against what shipped.",
